  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math> <mi>M</mi> </math> be a <math> <mrow> <mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow> </math> invertible matrix with real entries and let <math> <mi>I</mi> </math> denote the <math> <mrow> <mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow> </math> identity matrix. <math> <mrow> <msup> <mi>M</mi> <mrow> <mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </msup> <mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mfenced> <mrow> <mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>M</mi></mrow> </mfenced></mrow> </math>, then which of the following statements is/are ALWAYS TRUE?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "78ak2",
      "text": "<math> <mrow>  <mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></math>",
